ist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.0408530964475265,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.7129956426222439,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.028697634868719464,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":26.2,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.050479024571425404,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":50.2,"_gate_pool_share":-0.04604786404250194,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":21.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.14333777758703103,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":96.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.1076582788286935,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":78.8,"_gate_margins":0.002435415616407699,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":52.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04889672710813271,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":65.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.07721278761790673,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012366597425387876,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":79.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00456,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ICON Public Limited Company, a clinical research organization, provides outsourced development and commercialization services in Ireland, Europe, the United States, and internationally. The company specializes in the strategic development, management, and analysis of programs that support various stages of the clinical development process from compound selection to Phase I-IV clinical studies. It also provides clinical development services, including all phases of development, peri and post approval, data solutions, and site and patient access services; clinical trial management, consulting, contract staffing, data solutions, and laboratory services; and commercial services comprising clinical development strategy, planning and trial design, full study execution, and post-market commercialization. In addition, the company offers testing services comprising bioanalytical, biomarker, vaccine, good manufacturing practice, and central laboratory services, as well as full-service and functional service partnerships to customers. Further, the company provides adaptive trials, cardiac safety solutions, clinical and scientific operations, consulting and advisory, commercial positioning, decentralized and hybrid clinical trials, early clinical, medical imaging, real world intelligence, site and patient, and strategic solutions. Additionally, it provides therapeutics for cardiovascular, central nervous system, endocrine and metabolic disorders, hepatology, infectious diseases, internal medicine immunology, and oncology. It serves pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and medical device industries, as well as government and public health organizations. ICON Public Limited Company was incorporated in 1989 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Barry  Balfe | CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $985,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 40K people. Revenue per employee of $205K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["ICON plc is a large-cap healthcare business with a $15.3B market cap on $8.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $862M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 54% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 135% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3546332046332048},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ICON (ICLR) Launches FIRECREST AI Video Engine For Clinical Trial Communications","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-iclr/icon/news/icon-iclr-launches-firecrest-ai-video-engine-for-clinical-tr","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793975263.357,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Icon (NASDAQ:ICLR) Director Ciaran Murray Sells 3,452 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/icon-nasdaqiclr-director-ciaran-murray-sells-3452-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793879631.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Icon (NASDAQ:ICLR) CAO Emer Lyons Sells 264 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/icon-nasdaqiclr-cao-emer-lyons-sells-264-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793748530.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ICON PLC (ICLR) Is Leveraging AI to Accelerate Clinical Trials","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/icon-plc-iclr-leveraging-ai-154952795.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793720992.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ICON (ICLR) Stock Still Offers A Cash Flow Bargain","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us